>&#x02013;92.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8638942</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="journal">Nisoli, E., E. Clementi, C. Paolucci, V. Cozzi, C. Tonello, C. Sciorati, R. Bracale, A. Valerio, M. Francolini, S. Moncada, and M.O. Carruba. <year>2003</year>. Mitochondrial biogenesis in mammals: the role of endogenous nitric oxide. <source>Science.</source> <volume>299</volume>:<fpage>896</fpage>&#x02013;899.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12574632</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib29"><label>29</label><citation citation-type="journal">Nisoli, E., S. Falcone, C. Tonello, V. Cozzi, L. Palomba, M. Fiorani, A. Pisconti, S. Brunelli, A. Cardile, M. Francolini, et al. <year>2004</year>. Mitochondrial biogenesis by NO yields functionally active mitochondria in mammals. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>101</volume>:<fpage>16507</fpage>&#x02013;16512.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15545607</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib30"><label>30</label><citation citation-type="journal">Brookes, P.S., E.P. Salinas, K. Darley-Usmar, J.P. Eiserich, B.A. Freeman, V.M. Darley-Usmar, and P.G. Anderson. <year>2000</year>. Concentration-dependent effects of nitric oxide on mitochondrial permeability transition and cytochrome c release. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>275</volume>:<fpage>20474</fpage>&#x02013;20479.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10791954</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib31"><label>31</label><citation citation-type="journal">Kim, Y.M., T.H. Kim, D.W. Seol, R.V. Talanian, and T.R. Billiar. <year>1998</year>. Nitric oxide suppression of apoptosis occurs in association with an inhibition of Bcl-2 cleavage and cytochrome c release. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>273</volume>:<fpage>31437</fpage>&#x02013;31441.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9813055</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib32"><label>32</label><citation citation-type="journal">Yellon, D.M., and J.M. Downey. <year>2003</year>. Preconditioning the myo